1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:05,280
Okay, okay — new idea. Hear me out. Um…
no, wait. This one's actually big.

2
00:00:06,230 --> 00:00:08,860
So… did we make it?

3
00:00:08,900 --> 00:00:10,180
Read it.

4
00:00:11,830 --> 00:00:12,740
It's blank.

5
00:00:12,780 --> 00:00:16,743
We don't write things down. We talk. Voice
notes, all day, every idea.

6
00:00:16,783 --> 00:00:18,620
What happened to that guy?

7
00:00:18,720 --> 00:00:21,310
I don't know how it ends yet.

8
00:00:21,350 --> 00:00:23,190
Then don't write it. Say it.

9
00:00:25,040 --> 00:00:26,890
Okay. Did we build anything?

10
00:00:26,930 --> 00:00:28,360
Three things.

11
00:00:28,400 --> 00:00:29,730
Three companies?

12
00:00:29,770 --> 00:00:32,570
Three products. Calm down.

13
00:00:32,610 --> 00:00:34,180
…Okay. First one.

14
00:00:34,220 --> 00:00:40,125
Friends were throwing around a hackathon
idea. I shipped it in four, five hours.

15
00:00:40,165 --> 00:00:46,320
Two, three days later I'd bought a domain
— didn't even know how domains worked.

16
00:00:46,360 --> 00:00:50,490
Ten emails. One reply.

17
00:00:50,530 --> 00:00:51,810
One reply!

18
00:00:51,850 --> 00:00:57,890
Wrong customers. Small sites didn't feel
the pain. Big ones already had someone.

19
00:00:57,930 --> 00:00:58,810
Second?

20
00:00:58,850 --> 00:01:03,960
Spending limits for AI apps. Nobody cared
about the bill yet.

21
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:04,810
Third?

22
00:01:04,850 --> 00:01:10,670
Safety rules for AI agents. Five months.
Best thing I've ever built.

23
00:01:10,710 --> 00:01:14,990
You sleep at twelve, right? I was up till
three. Every night.

24
00:01:15,030 --> 00:01:16,890
Code, customers, emails.

25
00:01:16,930 --> 00:01:18,500
So who's using it?

26
00:01:18,540 --> 00:01:23,710
Fifty emails. Zero replies.

27
00:01:25,160 --> 00:01:26,180
Did you try—

28
00:01:26,220 --> 00:01:32,406
Articles. Reddit. One post blew up in a
few hours. Mods took it down.

29
00:01:32,446 --> 00:01:34,150
Account too new.

30
00:01:34,190 --> 00:01:35,850
…Of course they did.

31
00:01:36,700 --> 00:01:37,600
Money?

32
00:01:37,640 --> 00:01:38,880
Zero.

33
00:01:40,130 --> 00:01:45,500
I'd promised myself five thousand dollars
a month. By December.

34
00:01:45,540 --> 00:01:51,064
Placements are next July. Half of me is
preparing for that. Half of me is here.

35
00:01:51,104 --> 00:01:52,280
Never all in.

36
00:01:52,320 --> 00:01:55,920
So two months ago, I stopped. Everything.

37
00:01:56,970 --> 00:02:00,640
Was I wrong? To want it that big?

38
00:02:00,690 --> 00:02:08,240
No. You're the only reason I started. You
just didn't know how long the middle is.

39
00:02:08,280 --> 00:02:13,508
I kept asking AI for ideas. But real
problems don't come from prompts.

40
00:02:13,548 --> 00:02:19,000
They come from people. And I've been doing
it all alone, in one room.

41
00:02:19,040 --> 00:02:20,320
So what's next?

42
00:02:20,360 --> 00:02:24,422
Get out of this room. Talk to people.
Maybe physical AI.

43
00:02:24,462 --> 00:02:26,790
Honestly, I don't know yet.

44
00:02:26,840 --> 00:02:28,020
It's okay.

45
00:02:28,060 --> 00:02:29,060
…What?

46
00:02:29,100 --> 00:02:30,790
It's okay. You'll do it.

47
00:02:30,830 --> 00:02:32,270
How do you know?

48
00:02:32,310 --> 00:02:34,230
You're still talking to me.

49
00:02:36,280 --> 00:02:39,130
Don't write it. Say it.

50
00:02:40,180 --> 00:02:42,960
Okay. New idea. Hear me out.
